==French==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/kɔ.pɛ̃/|lang=fr}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|fr}} {{term/t|fro|compain}}, {{term/t|fro|cumpain}}, from {{etyl|LL.|fr}} {{term/t|la|compāniō}} (nominative form), from {{prefix|com|pānis|lang=la}} (literally, [[with]] + [[bread]]), a word first attested in the {{etyl|frk|-}} ''Lex Salica'' as a translation of a Germanic word, probably {{etyl|frk|en}} {{term/t|frk|*galaibo}}, {{term/t|frk|*gahlaibo||messmate|lit=with-bread}}, from {{term/t|frk|*hlaib||loaf, bread}}. See also {{term/t|fr|compagnon}}, from the accusative form of the Late Latin term (''compāniōnem''), from whence also English {{term|companion|lang=en}}. The boyfriend meaning is by ellipsis of {{term|petit copain|lang=fr}}

===Noun===
{{fr-noun|m|f=copine}}

#  (male) [[friend]], [[chum]], [[mate]] (''UK''), [[pal]]
# {{context|informal|lang=fr}} [[boyfriend]] {{gloss|boy/man to which one has a romantic attachment}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|male friend}} [[ami]]
* {{sense|boyfriend}} [[petit ami]], [[ami]]

